  "name": "Pokémon Happy Adventure Rally 2002",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Happy Adventure Rally 2002 was JR East's Pokémon rally that year, one of the rallies it has run at Tokyo stations since 1997. Participants collected six Pokémon Card e cards, 042 to 047/P, at stations of Tokyo's Yamanote Line and at Pokémon Center Tokyo, and found the goal station from hints left at special points.\n\nMidori Harada drew all six, Celebi, Entei, Pikachu, Pichu, Mewtwo and Lugia, and their pictures join into one scene. Each has an attack or Poké-Power whose name contains \"Link\", such as Celebi's Para Link and Pikachu's Smash Link.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "ポケモンスタンプラリーSta.: ポケモンスタンプラリー 開催の記録",
